Note it's supposed to be the quotes in the object:

[someProp]="{'a': x}"
aObject(x: any) { return {'a': x}; }

> Thus the object is recreated only when x changes

yeah, you are right.

> With the workaround it is recreated on each check, considered changed and repopulated in the DOM.

```
class MyComp {
  private _myObj = {'a': x};
  aObject(x: any) { return this._myObj; }
}
```
